Support QEMU's e1000 (Intel 82540EM) alongside a real Ophir (82571).

A dropin binding for device-id 0x100e -- no real Ophir reports that -- routes
QEMU's e1000 to this driver. A `qemu-e1000?` predicate (config offset 0,
device-id == 0x100e) then selects, per site, the behaviour QEMU's model needs
without disturbing the 82571 path.

reg-property-value: QEMU's 82540EM has a 32-bit memory BAR0 at 0x10 and a
separate I/O BAR1 at 0x14, and Solaris e1000g needs that I/O BAR for an 82540
or fails to attach ("Mapping registers failed"). Under qemu-e1000? the reg
describes that layout; otherwise it stays the 82571's single 64-bit BAR0.

Applied to the build tree, not src/obp -- but it no longer misdescribes a
real 82571, so it could move into src/obp with a marker if wanted.

--- a/obp/dev/network/ophir/load.fth	2026-09-08 22:10:18.555237252 +0200
+++ b/obp/dev/network/ophir/load.fth	2026-09-08 22:10:18.585237429 +0200
@@ -50,9 +50,24 @@
    >r encode-phys 0 encode-int encode+ r> encode-int encode+
 ;
 
+: qemu-e1000?	( -- flag )
+   \ True for QEMU's e1000 model (Intel 82540EM, device-id 0x100e). No real
+   \ Ophir/82571 reports 0x100e, so this alone tells the two apart. Read
+   \ config offset 0 direct -- config-access.fth is not fload'ed yet here.
+   0 my-space or " config-l@" $call-parent  d# 16 rshift  h# 100e  =
+;
+
 : reg-property-value	( -- adr len )
    my-address my-space 0 encode-reg
-   my-address my-space h# 300.0010 or h# 2.0000 encode-reg encode+
+   qemu-e1000? if
+      \ QEMU 82540EM: 32-bit memory BAR0 at 0x10, separate I/O BAR1 at 0x14.
+      \ Solaris e1000g requires that I/O BAR for an 82540 or fails to attach.
+      my-address my-space h# 200.0010 or h# 2.0000 encode-reg encode+
+      my-address my-space h# 100.0014 or h#      40 encode-reg encode+
+   else
+      \ Real 82571: one 64-bit memory BAR0 spanning 0x10 and 0x14.
+      my-address my-space h# 300.0010 or h# 2.0000 encode-reg encode+
+   then
 ;
 
 \ General Includes
--- a/obp/arch/sun4v/niagara1-hw/release/dropins.src	2026-09-08 22:10:18.572237353 +0200
+++ b/obp/arch/sun4v/niagara1-hw/release/dropins.src	2026-09-08 22:10:42.247377024 +0200
@@ -212,6 +212,16 @@
    \ not used on plugin cards.
    alias pciex8086,1060.8086.105e pciex8086,105e.108e.105e
 
+   \ QEMU's e1000 model: 8086:100e, an 82540EM. Not an Ophir, but it answers
+   \ the same register block -- bit-banged EEPROM at EEC, MDIC PHY access,
+   \ and the legacy descriptor rings -- and its PHY is a plain MII one, which
+   \ is all phy.fth asks for. The EEPROM warning above does not apply: under
+   \ QEMU the EEPROM is synthesised per boot from the -device macaddr, so
+   \ there is no card to brick.
+   : pci8086,100e.1af4.1100 ( -- )
+      " ophir" load-driver
+   ;
+
 }source
 
